  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Activity under preparation West Africa/Sierra Leone/Education Skills Skills Development infrastructure for value chain upgrading</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;color: rgb(21, 96, 130);&quot;&gt;This grant would support Sierra Leone&#xbf;s national development priorities and the EU Global Gateway strategy, focusing on enhancing connectivity through strategic infrastructure investments in West African trading corridors. A key initiative under this framework is the rehabilitation of key feeder roads through the EU funded Opportunity Salone project, launched in 2021, implemented by the ILO and its partners in Sierra Leone. Improved infrastructure is a precondition for ACFTA.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;color: rgb(21, 96, 130);&quot;&gt;Activities&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;color: rgb(21, 96, 130);&quot;&gt;Taking a 360-degree approach the additional funding will contribute to ensuring that (i) investments in roads and (ii) selected agricultural value chains are sustainable, benefit local communities and are embedded in a conducive institutional framework. The ILO proposes to expand the current project by strengthening skills institutions, methodologies and systems. Activities will include: &lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;ol&gt;&lt;li data-list=&quot;bullet&quot;&gt;&lt;span class=&quot;ql-ui&quot; contenteditable=&quot;false&quot;&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;color: rgb(21, 96, 130);&quot;&gt;Creating a regular mechanism for &lt;/span&gt;&lt;strong style=&quot;color: rgb(21, 96, 130);&quot;&gt;identifying critical skills gaps&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;color: rgb(21, 96, 130);&quot;&gt; both for road infrastructure support as well as specific skills that can help enhancing the ecosystem fort entrepreneurship and for agricultural sector development. Making sure both public and private sector needs are captured and developing a framework of how this information can inform and guide the TVET, entrepreneurship and private training system and offer, as for providers to update and develop relevant curricula.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/li&gt;&lt;li data-list=&quot;bullet&quot;&gt;&lt;span class=&quot;ql-ui&quot; contenteditable=&quot;false&quot;&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;color: rgb(21, 96, 130);&quot;&gt;Developing one or two &lt;/span&gt;&lt;strong style=&quot;color: rgb(21, 96, 130);&quot;&gt;national/regional centres for vocational excellence for labour-based works in road construction and maintenance and for agrifood products&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;color: rgb(21, 96, 130);&quot;&gt;, in close collaboration with the private sector. These centres will focus on delivering quality and market-relevant skills training and will serve as hubs for opportunity driven skills development, including on skills relevant for on employment intensive investments and road maintenance. &lt;/span&gt;&lt;/li&gt;&lt;li data-list=&quot;bullet&quot;&gt;&lt;span class=&quot;ql-ui&quot; contenteditable=&quot;false&quot;&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;color: rgb(21, 96, 130);&quot;&gt;Ensuring that workers in labour-based construction work acquire skills and receive government approved &lt;/span&gt;&lt;strong style=&quot;color: rgb(21, 96, 130);&quot;&gt;certification&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;color: rgb(21, 96, 130);&quot;&gt; at the end of their contract, plus soft, &lt;/span&gt;&lt;strong style=&quot;color: rgb(21, 96, 130);&quot;&gt;entrepreneurial and agro-processing relevant skills&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;color: rgb(21, 96, 130);&quot;&gt;, to enhance their employability and career prospects. This will be achieved through a network of TVET centres and business development service providers supporting graduates.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/li&gt;&lt;li data-list=&quot;bullet&quot;&gt;&lt;span class=&quot;ql-ui&quot; contenteditable=&quot;false&quot;&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;color: rgb(21, 96, 130);&quot;&gt;Reviewing and &lt;/span&gt;&lt;strong style=&quot;color: rgb(21, 96, 130);&quot;&gt;improving regulatory frameworks&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;color: rgb(21, 96, 130);&quot;&gt; to include skills certification by relevant government partners (Ministry of Technical and Higher Education). &lt;/span&gt;&lt;/li&gt;&lt;li data-list=&quot;bullet&quot;&gt;&lt;span class=&quot;ql-ui&quot; contenteditable=&quot;false&quot;&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;color: rgb(21, 96, 130);&quot;&gt;Reviewing and &lt;/span&gt;&lt;strong style=&quot;color: rgb(21, 96, 130);&quot;&gt;improving governance and financing arrangements&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;color: rgb(21, 96, 130);&quot;&gt; for inclusive skills development, so that skills development provision can flexibly react to investment opportunities.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/li&gt;&lt;/ol&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;/p&gt;</narrative>
  </description>
